<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Silla–Tang War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">670–676</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Silla–Tang War was fought from 670 to 676 between the Korean kingdom of Silla and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>, its former ally against Baekje and Goguryeo. Silla resisted Tang plans to rule the conquered lands and supported Goguryeo rebels. After Silla's victories at Maeso Fortress in 675 and Gibeolpo in 676, the Tang withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, and Silla controlled the peninsula south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taedong-river">Taedong River</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/silla-tang-war.jpg" alt="Silla–Tang War" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EB%82%98%EB%8B%B9%EC%A0%84%EC%9F%81%EA%B3%BC_%EB%B3%B4%EB%8D%95%EA%B5%AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
